<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jaluit Atoll</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jaluit is a coral atoll in the Ralik chain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marshall-islands">Marshall Islands</a> in the central Pacific. German traders based their copra business there, and from 1885 it was the administrative centre of the German Marshall Islands <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a>. Under Japanese rule after 1914 it remained the main administrative seat and became a military base in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jaluit-atoll.jpg" alt="Jaluit Atoll" width="320" height="253" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: NASA Johnson Space Center - Earth Sciences and Image Analysis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jaluit.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
